  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study relies entirely on qualitative institutional documents and project materials rather than direct observational or experiential data from the participants of these care initiatives.",
      "what": "This study analyzes how care is integrated into urban space by examining four active initiatives in Montevideo, Uruguay: the Plan Nacional de Cuidados, Cuidados en el B, Fincas Recuperadas, and Reactor. Using a qualitative analysis of institutional documents and project materials, the research investigates how these programs reorganize social reproduction through communal practices and everyday urban arrangements.",
      "why": "It demonstrates how the intersection of national policy frameworks and neighborhood-scale interventions can move care beyond simple social assistance, reframing access to housing, services, and public space as collective responsibilities."
